From a95809ff6927217f30579c883e89b36cc83c1337 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:38:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] storage: DomA's block read-ahead at 512 KiB

init.xenvm-readahead.rc writes 512 to read_ahead_kb of vda and of the dm
devices (dm-0 to dm-15; init's write takes no wildcard, this board has
had up to dm-9, and one that does not exist fails harmlessly) instead of
the 8192 KiB they come up with on this board. It writes them at
post-fs-data, after late-fs, because /data sits on a dm device of its
own (metadata encryption) that mount_all --late creates. The product
makefile installs it, and README.md lists it.

DomA's disk is virtio-blk served by qemu in DomD, and without ioeventfd
the device model maps each request's guest memory on its main loop with
the BQL held: one 8 MiB read-ahead request took about 20 ms there,
longer than a frame, and qemu's time budget for virtio-blk cannot split
a single request. Measured on this board with the value set at run time
(2026-10-25): the virtio-blk holds over the frame time went away under a
cold read of the disk, and in the 580 s runs of a WebView's 720p60
H.264 the main loop held the BQL for a vsync or more only with single
GPU commands. That init writes it from this rc has not been run on the
board yet. The Raspberry Pi 5 product keeps the kernel's default.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [automotive-grade-linux/Android_device_sodev_xenvm-cf]
